hat the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<div class=\"page\">\n  <div class=\"stack gap-lg\" style=\"max-width:420px;margin:48px auto;\">\n    <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n      <h1>Sign in</h1>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Welcome back. Enter your email and password to access your account.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <form class=\"stack gap-lg\" onsubmit=\"event.preventDefault(); document.getElementById('login-error').style.display='none'; const e=this.email.value.trim(); const p=this.password.value; if(!/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(e)||p.length<8){document.getElementById('login-error').style.display='block';} else {document.getElementById('login-success').style.display='block';}\">\n        <div id=\"login-error\" class=\"alert alert-destructive\" style=\"display:none;\">\n          <strong>We couldn't sign you in.</strong> Check that your email is valid and your password is at least 8 characters.\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"login-success\" class=\"alert\" style=\"display:none;\">\n          Form validated. Connect this to your authentication service to complete sign-in.\n        </div>\n\n        <label class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n          <span>Email</span>\n          <input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" place